Monthly acquisition holdouts now update the cost of each opportunity. \VAR{b_runner} also has a positive point estimate, but its cost uncertainty warrants keeping expansion on hold while testing continues. Current first-year value estimates do not support scaling either save-time campaign at its tested cost.

\Section{The investment case depends on value and timing}
The acquisition tests counted additional buyers. The value projection assumes those buyers follow the matching customer group's contribution path. For \VAR{b_best}, that implies recovering iCAC at the \VAR{b_best_payback}th monthly payment. Roughly half of its first-year value is forecast, so expansion should be accompanied by monitoring of the acquired cohorts' renewal and contribution.

