\ReportEntry{01\quad Studio North and the customer journey}
\PageTitle{01 / THE BUSINESS}{Studio North and the\newline customer journey}{A monthly membership helps independent professionals finish work and build creative skills.}
Members pay for access to templates and guided learning, with standard and premium plans plus optional add-ons. They renew when the benefits continue to justify the next payment. Contribution is payment revenue after discounts, refunds and recorded delivery costs; it funds acquisition and the rest of the business.

\ReportFigure{business-journey}{Conceptual journey through the membership: potential benefits and friction around an expected experience. The curve illustrates a hypothesis about experience, not a measured sentiment score.}{business-journey.png}{4.1in}
\Section{Two reasons to join, two patterns of value}
A save-time member may seek a quick solution to a task. A build-skill member may return to make progress over several months. Those stated needs give management a practical starting point for segmentation.

The journey perspective follows \SourceCite{course2026}{Tian (2026)}. Detailed activity and feedback diagnostics appear in Appendix C. Tables~\ref{tab:ucv-people}--\ref{tab:ucv-channel-holdouts} in Appendix E catalogue the eight sources and their customer-view fields.

