\Section{The value assumption is the key condition}
The experiments establish additional acquisitions, not those buyers' subsequent value. \VAR{b_best} needs about \VAR{b_best_break_even} of its benchmark value to break even at point iCAC; \VAR{b_runner} needs about \VAR{b_runner_break_even}. These thresholds give management a concrete way to assess the risk of acquiring a different customer mix.

\Section{The two build-skill opportunities warrant different steps}
Prioritize \VAR{b_best} for a measured expansion once Finance has set the cash limit. Its iCAC interval is \VAR{b_best_ci}, below the \VAR{b_best_value} value benchmark. For \VAR{b_runner}, the \VAR{b_runner_ci} interval spans its \VAR{b_runner_value} benchmark. Keep its expansion on hold while the monthly program measures the next acquisition price.

Current point estimates do not support scaling the save-time campaigns. A lower tested acquisition price or a stronger contribution benchmark would change that conclusion.

\Section{What the latest leading test implies in dollars}
Applying the benchmark to \VAR{b_best_extra_buyers} additional buyers gives about \VAR{b_best_total_value} of first-year contribution value. Less \VAR{b_pilot_spend} of acquisition spending, the planning surplus is approximately \VAR{b_best_total_net}. This is the economic case to monitor as the acquisition program expands.

\NewPage
\ReportEntry{09\quad Management action}
\PageTitle{09 / MANAGEMENT ACTION}{Make acquisition testing\newline part of the monthly review}{Update the acquisition price, then choose spending against customer value and cash timing.}
\Section{Marketing and Finance: agree the first expansion}
Give \VAR{b_best} priority. Finance should choose an affordable spending step and the acceptable recovery period. The benchmark planning case recovers iCAC at payment \VAR{b_best_payback}; the historical payment-\VAR{b_best_historical_payback} recovery does not fund the same investment.

\Section{Marketing and Analytics: renew the evidence monthly}
Enroll fresh prospects each month and preserve each assignment for the full 31-day window. When results close, update iCAC for every channel--need cell, including unfavorable results. Keep holdouts when spending, audience or campaign changes so the acquisition price reflects the next operating conditions. Maintain capped research spending while holding broader expansion of \VAR{b_runner} and the save-time campaigns.

\Section{Product and Operations: make recurring value visible}
Use stated need to distinguish immediate task completion from ongoing skill development. Track time to first useful outcome and reasons for cancellation. The current completion and activity flags provide little separation in subsequent renewal, so richer experience measures would help explain why cohorts improve.

\Section{Analytics and Finance: refresh the investment case}
Bring the latest completed iCAC, its uncertainty and the recurring research budget to each spending review. Update contribution benchmarks as operating cohorts mature, then recalculate value less iCAC and cash recovery. Track new cohorts' customer mix and contribution against the assumptions supporting expansion.

\Takeaway{Give \VAR{b_best} the next measured expansion. Reassess that priority as monthly holdouts update acquisition cost and maturing cohorts update contribution value.}

